meta {
  name: Confirm Booking
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/public/booking-confirmations/confirm
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "{{confirmationToken}}"
  }
}

docs {
  The patient's click on "Confirmar mi cita". Same body and token as View Confirmation. Idempotent:
  confirming twice answers the current view.

  In auto-confirm mode the booking is created (matching or creating the patient, recording consent) and
  the view is `confirmed`. With `REQUIRE_APPROVAL`, or when the contact matches an inactive or deleted
  patient, the request goes to the provider's inbox and the view is `requested`. An expired hold answers
  `expired`; a click that cannot be honoured answers 409 (slot taken, including by the provider, who is
  never blocked by an unconfirmed hold; booking cap; in approval mode "Request limit reached" when the
  contact already has 3 live requests) or 404 (booking paused, type or location no longer offered) and
  releases the hold; the view is then `unavailable`. 404 for an unknown token.
}
